A directory given as `input` and as `./input` lists each of its files once: the glob view lists display paths in a lexical normal form (no `.` or empty segments), so `./input/a.md` and `input/a.md` are one line, printed as `input/a.md`. The first line keeps the arguments as given.
== args
input
./input
== file input/a.md
# A
== file input/sub/b.md
# B
== stdout
glob view: input ./input
input/a.md (1 line): # A
input/sub/b.md (1 line): # B
== stderr
== exit 0
